## Attempt 1 (session `coord1`) -- glm-cli: real, deterministic config-tier stop (honest, not a session-engine/dispatch defect, and NOT this cell's bug)

```
node p032-live-proof-driver-script.mjs coord_p032_live_<ts>_glm glm-cli open
node p032-live-proof-driver-script.mjs coord_p032_live_<ts>_glm glm-cli request
```
Transcripts: `glm-cli-step1-open.std{out,err}.log`, `glm-cli-step2-request.std{out,err}.log`.

`openDeclaredProtocolSession` succeeded (real `.fgos/coordination/sessions/
coord_p032_live_<ts>_glm/session.json`/`events.jsonl` written, both
`requester-actor`/`consultant-actor` bound). `dispatchDeclaredOperation`
(`request-consult`, `cliPolicy: { preferExecutor: 'glm-cli', minTier:
'lightweight' }`) genuinely materialized ONE real Assignment
(`asgn_p03_2_live_proof_coordinator_op_001`, confirmed in
`coord1-glm-codex-attempts-events.jsonl` seq 4 and
`coord1-glm-codex-attempts-session.json`'s `assignmentRefs`) but threw
BEFORE any subprocess ever spawned:
```
RunnerConfigError: no model configured for policy tier "standard" under provider "z-ai".
    at resolvePolicyTierModel ... at resolveAssignmentDispatchPolicy ...
    at compileDispatchPlan ... at executeAssignment ...
    at createAndExecuteSessionTask (session-engine.mjs:257)
    at dispatchDeclaredOperation (session-engine.mjs:1149)
```

**Root cause, confirmed by reading source directly (not guessed):**
`assignment-policy.mjs:92`'s `effectiveTier = opPolicy.minTier || 'standard'`
is an unconditional, pre-existing, system-wide floor -- `'standard'` unless
the Assignment's OWN declared policy sets something else, and `minTier` is
monotonic RAISE-ONLY (`resolveStrongerTier`/`strength()`,
`assignment-policy.mjs:121-122`): a caller-supplied `minTier` LOWER than the
current effective value is silently ignored, never lowers it. `.fgos/config.json`'s
`modelPolicies.z-ai` has only a `lightweight` entry -- no `standard` --
so ANY declared-path dispatch through `glm-cli`, for ANY operation
(`request-consult` has no operation-level `minTier` either, so it inherits
the SAME `'standard'` system floor), is structurally blocked. Confirmed this
is not a fixable-by-caller condition for the DECLARED path specifically: the
agent-led path's own `opts.cliOverride.model` (a raw pass-through field,
`P01.2`'s own documented workaround for the identical class of stop against
`codex-cli`) bypasses tier-based model lookup entirely -- but the declared
path's `cliPolicy`/`resolveDeclaredPolicyStack` funnels every caller
preference through `mergePolicyStack`'s PolicyPatch schema
(`definitions/schema.mjs:66`,
`POLICY_PATCH_FIELDS = {minTier, preferPersona, preferExecutor,
fallbackExecutors, visibility}`), which has NO `model` field at all --
confirmed by reading the schema directly. This is not a bug introduced by
this cell: `assignment-policy.mjs`'s floor default predates P03.2 and is
outside this cell's touchable surface (`src/runner/dispatch/**` is Do-Not-
Touch); the declared path's PolicyPatch schema omitting a literal `model`
field is itself R1's own by-design constraint ("a portable protocol...
expresses requirements... never a literal executor/model pin"), just with
the previously-undocumented side effect that it also removes the ONE escape
hatch that makes a `lightweight`-only-configured provider (`z-ai`, `gemini`,
`openai-codex`) reachable at all when an operation's effective tier resolves
to `standard`. Worth a documentation note for a future cell, not a fix
folded into this one (`.fgos/config.json` and `definitions/schema.mjs` are
both outside P03.2's file ownership).

