## Attempt 3 (session `coord1`, requester Assignment) -- claude: genuine live dispatch, but a SELF-INFLICTED methodology false-fail (kept as honest evidence, not hidden)

```
node p032-live-proof-driver-script.mjs coord_p032_live_<ts>_glm claude request
```
Transcript: `claude-attempt-self-inflicted-dirty-tree-false-fail.std{out,err}.log`.

A REAL `claude` CLI subprocess genuinely spawned, read the real
`package.json`, and answered correctly (`agentClaim.status: "done"`,
`agentClaim.summary`: "Repository root package.json name is \"forgent\",
version is \"0.1.0\"." -- the real, correct answer). But the persisted
`RunResult` classified as `status: "failed", confidence: "failed"`, NOT
`"done"`. Traced the cause directly, not guessed:
`evidence.mutatedDirtyBeforeFiles` listed exactly one path -- THIS proof's
own `claude-step3-request-live.stderr.log`, which my own shell redirect
(`2> docs/.../proofs/P03.2/....stderr.log`) was writing INTO the tracked
repo tree WHILE the Assignment's real-time mutation-freshness check
(`assignment-runner.mjs`'s `mutatedDirtyBeforeFiles`/`hasDirtyBeforeMutation`,
unmodified by this cell) was watching for exactly this shape of change
against a read-only Assignment. This is a genuine, correctly-firing
governance mechanism (P03.2 did not touch or weaken it) tripped by this
proof's OWN test-harness log placement, not a session-engine/coordination
defect -- confirmed by re-running the identical dispatch with stdout/stderr
redirected OUTSIDE the repo tree (Attempt 4 below), which completed
`status: "done"` with byte-identical `agentClaim` content. Kept here,
unmodified, as required honest evidence rather than deleted/hidden; every
subsequent live attempt in this proof redirects output to the scratchpad
directory during the dispatch itself, copying transcripts into this
directory only AFTER the assignment settles.

