## Summary

R8's live-proof requirement is met with `claude` as the real registered
executor: `request-consult` -> `provide-consult` -> `recordConsultDisposition`
all completed genuinely (`status: "done"`, `confidence: "reported"`, real,
mutually-consistent, independently-reasoned answers; zero repository
mutation; zero direct executor launch outside `executeAssignment()`).
`glm-cli`/`codex-cli` (the two executors P00.3/P01.2 used for their own live
proofs) were both genuinely attempted first and both hit the SAME real,
deterministic, pre-existing config-tier gap (a `standard`-tier floor with no
matching `modelPolicies` entry for either provider family, and no
model-override escape hatch reachable through the declared path's own
PolicyPatch schema) -- honestly documented as legitimate, non-fabricated
partial evidence, not routed around or hidden, matching this track's
established precedent for handling a genuine live-executor/config
limitation. The one methodology false-fail (Attempt 3, this proof's own log
file sitting inside the watched repo tree during a read-only dispatch) is
kept unmodified as evidence and traced to its real cause rather than
silently deleted or re-run without explanation.
